      "response": [
        {
          "value": "The `$LASTEXITCODE` variable in PowerShell holds the exit code of the last native executable that was run in the session. It does not apply to PowerShell cmdlets or functions but only to external executables invoked from PowerShell.\n\nIn your script, `$LASTEXITCODE` is likely being set by the `dotnet` command or another external executable invoked earlier in the script. Specifically, the `dotnet` command (e.g., `dotnet --info`) might be returning an exit code of `26`.\n\n### Steps to Investigate:\n1. **Check the `dotnet` Command**:\n   - Run `dotnet --info` manually in the terminal and check its exit code using `$LASTEXITCODE` immediately after.\n   - Example:\n     ```powershell\n     dotnet --info\n     $LASTEXITCODE\n     ```\n\n2. **Interpret the Exit Code**:\n   - Exit codes are specific to the executable. For `dotnet`, exit codes are not well-documented for all scenarios, but a non-zero exit code typically indicates an error or issue.\n   - Common causes for non-zero exit codes in `dotnet` include:\n     - Missing or corrupted .NET SDK or runtime.\n     - Misconfigured environment variables (e.g., `DOTNET_ROOT`).\n     - Permission issues accessing required files or directories.\n\n3. **Debugging the Issue**:\n   - Ensure the `dotnet` executable is accessible and functioning correctly.\n   - Verify that the paths (e.g., `$env:ProgramFiles\\dotnet`) and required files exist.\n   - Check for any error messages or warnings in the output of `dotnet --info`.\n\n### What Exit Code `26` Might Mean:\nWhile `dotnet` does not officially document an exit code `26`, it could indicate:\n- A specific runtime or SDK issue.\n- A problem with the environment configuration.\n\nIf the issue persists, consider:\n- Updating the .NET SDK and runtime to the latest version.\n- Checking the system logs or running the command with verbose logging (e.g., `dotnet --info --verbosity detailed`).\n\nIf `$LASTEXITCODE` is not from `dotnet`, review other external executables invoked in the script to identify the source.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
      ],
