    {
      "requestId": "request_32228d9b-40e5-4ebf-9943-f7726d6efb56",
      "message": {
        "text": "how are nuget server configured to establish URIs (especially ports ) for their push and pull API endpoints",
        "parts": [
          {
            "range": {
              "start": 0,
              "endExclusive": 107
            },
            "editorRange": {
              "startLineNumber": 1,
              "startColumn": 1,
              "endLineNumber": 1,
              "endColumn": 108
            },
            "text": "how are nuget server configured to establish URIs (especially ports ) for their push and pull API endpoints",
            "kind": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      "variableData": {
        "variables": [
          {
            "kind": "file",
            "id": "vscode.implicit.viewport",
            "name": "file:NuGet.Config",
            "value": {
              "uri": {
                "$mid": 1,
                "fsPath": "c:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell\\Resources\\NuGet.Config",
                "_sep": 1,
                "external": "file:///c%3A/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/Resources/NuGet.Config",
                "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/Resources/NuGet.Config",
                "scheme": "file"
              },
              "range": {
                "startLineNumber": 1,
                "startColumn": 1,
                "endLineNumber": 42,
                "endColumn": 17
              }
            },
            "modelDescription": "User's current visible code"
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": [
        {
          "value": "NuGet servers (such as [NuGet.Server](https://learn.microsoft.com/nuget/hosting-packages/nuget-server), [BaGet](https://github.com/loic-sharma/BaGet), [Nexus](https://help.sonatype.com/repomanager3/nuget-repositories), [Artifactory](https://jfrog.com/help/r/jfrog-artifactory-documentation/nuget-repositories), or [Azure Artifacts](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/devops/artifacts/nuget/publish?view=azure-devops)) are configured independently of the NuGet client configuration. The URIs (including ports) for their push and pull endpoints are determined by the server's hosting and configuration, not by ",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "inlineReference",
          "inlineReference": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "fsPath": "c:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell\\Resources\\NuGet.Config",
            "_sep": 1,
            "external": "file:///c%3A/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/Resources/NuGet.Config",
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/Resources/NuGet.Config",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        },
        {
          "value": ".\n\n### How NuGet Servers Establish API Endpoint URIs\n\n#### 1. **Web Server Hosting**\n- Most NuGet servers are web applications (ASP.NET, .NET Core, etc.) hosted on a web server (IIS, Kestrel, Apache, Nginx, etc.).\n- The **base URI** (including port) is determined by the web server's configuration.\n  - Example:  \n    - IIS: Configured via site bindings (host, port, protocol).\n    - Kestrel: Configured via `appsettings.json` or command-line arguments (e.g., `--urls http://*:5000`).\n\n#### 2. **NuGet Server Application Configuration**\n- The NuGet server application may allow further configuration of the API path (e.g., `/nuget`, `/v3/index.json`).\n- Some servers allow you to set the repository path or virtual directory.\n\n#### 3. **Push and Pull Endpoints**\n- **Pull (Restore/Install):**  \n  The URI for pulling packages is typically the base URI plus the API path, e.g.:\n  ```\n  https://myserver:8081/nuget/v3/index.json\n  ```\n- **Push (Publish):**  \n  The push endpoint is usually the same base URI, but the server must support the NuGet push protocol (usually `/api/v2/package` for v2, or via the v3 protocol).\n\n#### 4. **Examples**\n- **NuGet.Server (ASP.NET):**\n  - Hosted in IIS at `http://myserver:8080/nuget`\n  - Pull: `http://myserver:8080/nuget/nuget`\n  - Push: `http://myserver:8080/nuget/api/v2/package`\n- **BaGet (Kestrel):**\n  - Hosted at `http://localhost:5000/v3/index.json`\n  - Push: `http://localhost:5000/api/v2/package`\n- **Artifactory/Nexus:**\n  - You configure the repository and its URL in the server's admin UI.\n  - Example: `https://artifacts.example.com/artifactory/api/nuget/nuget-local`\n\n#### 5. **Ports**\n- The port is set by the web server or container hosting the NuGet server.\n- Common ports: 80 (HTTP), 443 (HTTPS), or any custom port you specify.\n\n#### 6. **Discovery**\n- The NuGet client discovers the endpoints via the URL you provide in ",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "inlineReference",
          "inlineReference": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "fsPath": "c:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell\\Resources\\NuGet.Config",
            "_sep": 1,
            "external": "file:///c%3A/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/Resources/NuGet.Config",
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/Resources/NuGet.Config",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        },
        {
          "value": " or on the command line.\n- The server must be reachable at that URI and port.\n\n---\n\n**Summary:**  \nNuGet server endpoints (including ports) are established by the web server and the NuGet server application's configuration. The client (",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "inlineReference",
          "inlineReference": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "fsPath": "c:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell\\Resources\\NuGet.Config",
            "_sep": 1,
            "external": "file:///c%3A/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/Resources/NuGet.Config",
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/Resources/NuGet.Config",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        },
        {
          "value": ") just points to the server's published URI; it does not control or configure the server's endpoints or ports. Server admins must configure the server and hosting environment to expose the desired URIs and ports.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
      ],
