            {
              "code": "# Get the value of an environment variable from the current process\n$value = [Environment]::Get-EnvironmentVariable(\"VARIABLE_NAME\")\n\n# Example: Get the PATH variable\n$path = [Environment]::Get-EnvironmentVariable(\"PATH\")\n\n# To get a variable from a specific scope (Process, User, or Machine):\n$userVar = [Environment]::Get-EnvironmentVariable(\"VARIABLE_NAME\", \"User\")\n$machineVar = [Environment]::Get-EnvironmentVariable(\"VARIABLE_NAME\", \"Machine\")\n$processVar = [Environment]::Get-EnvironmentVariable(\"VARIABLE_NAME\", \"Process\")\n",
              "language": "powershell",
              "markdownBeforeBlock": "You can use `[Environment]::Get-EnvironmentVariable` in PowerShell to retrieve the value of an environment variable. Here’s the basic usage:\n\n"
