      "response": [
        {
          "value": "Yes, `[Environment]::Get-EnvironmentVariable($PSRepositoryFeedAPIKeyName)` is valid PowerShell syntax **if** `$PSRepositoryFeedAPIKeyName` contains the name of the environment variable as a string.\n\nHowever, the error you are seeing (`Unexpected token '-EnvironmentVariable' in expression or statement`) usually means there is a typo, missing bracket, or some other syntax issue **elsewhere** in your script, or you are running this line in a context where PowerShell is expecting a different kind of statement.\n\n**Example of correct usage:**\n```powershell\n$envVarName = 'NUGET_API_KEY'\n",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "markdownVuln",
          "content": {
            "value": "$",
            "supportThemeIcons": false,
            "supportHtml": false,
            "uris": {}
          },
          "vulnerabilities": [
            {
              "title": "hardcoded-credentials",
              "description": "Embedding credentials in source code risks unauthorized access"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "value": "apiKey = [Environment]::Get-EnvironmentVariable($envVarName)\nWrite-Host $apiKey\n```\n\n**Common mistakes:**\n- Accidentally typing a single colon (`:`) instead of double colons (`::`)\n- Misspelling the method name\n- Using this syntax in a context where PowerShell expects a cmdlet or statement, not a method call\n\n**Check:**\n- Make sure you are using `[Environment]::Get-EnvironmentVariable('VARNAME')` or `[Environment]::Get-EnvironmentVariable($varName)`\n- Make sure there are no typos or missing brackets in your code\n\n**If you still get the error,** please show the exact line and a few lines before and after it for more context.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
