              "language": "powershell",
              "markdownBeforeBlock": "Yes, `[Environment]::Get-EnvironmentVariable($PSRepositoryFeedAPIKeyName)` is valid PowerShell syntax **if** `$PSRepositoryFeedAPIKeyName` contains the name of the environment variable as a string.\n\nHowever, the error you are seeing (`Unexpected token '-EnvironmentVariable' in expression or statement`) usually means there is a typo, missing bracket, or some other syntax issue **elsewhere** in your script, or you are running this line in a context where PowerShell is expecting a different kind of statement.\n\n**Example of correct usage:**\n"
            }
