    {
      "requestId": "request_dc66c9cc-8201-4e0b-ab6b-79eee3213dfa",
      "message": {
        "text": "Where should the copilot instructions files direcotry be placed in a multi-project repository? Does every project root needs it's own copy of the instruction files, or, can a single directory be created at the root of the repository? ",
        "parts": [
          {
            "range": {
              "start": 0,
              "endExclusive": 234
            },
            "editorRange": {
              "startLineNumber": 1,
              "startColumn": 1,
              "endLineNumber": 1,
              "endColumn": 235
            },
            "text": "Where should the copilot instructions files direcotry be placed in a multi-project repository? Does every project root needs it's own copy of the instruction files, or, can a single directory be created at the root of the repository? ",
            "kind": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      "variableData": {
        "variables": [
          {
            "kind": "file",
            "id": "vscode.implicit.viewport",
            "name": "file:ReadMe.md",
            "value": {
              "uri": {
                "$mid": 1,
                "fsPath": "c:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell\\ReadMe.md",
                "_sep": 1,
                "external": "file:///c%3A/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/ReadMe.md",
                "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/ReadMe.md",
                "scheme": "file"
              },
              "range": {
                "startLineNumber": 90,
                "startColumn": 92,
                "endLineNumber": 111,
                "endColumn": 90
              }
            },
            "modelDescription": "User's current visible code"
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": [
        {
          "value": "You **do not need a copy of the Copilot instruction files in every project root**.  \nA **single `.copilot` directory at the root of your repository** is sufficient for GitHub Copilot to apply its instructions to all projects within that repository.\n\n**How it works:**\n- Copilot looks for a `.copilot` directory at the repository root.\n- All instructions in `.copilot` (e.g., `powershell.md`, `csharp.md`, `testing.md`) will apply to the entire repository and all its sub-projects.\n- You do **not** need to duplicate `.copilot` in each project folder.\n\n**Best practice:**  \nCreate and maintain a single `.copilot` directory at the root of your multi-project repository.\n\n**Reference:**  \n[GitHub Copilot Workspace Configuration](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/configuring-copilot/copilot-workspace-configuration)",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
      ],
