    {
      "requestId": "request_31a429d0-cdb8-4232-be8a-4a4aa76beebc",
      "message": {
        "text": "if there is a instructions directory at  the repository root, is their any hierarchal mechanism to support overriding the instructions or merging them with addition instructions placed at a project root or within a code-workpsace file in a project?",
        "parts": [
          {
            "range": {
              "start": 0,
              "endExclusive": 248
            },
            "editorRange": {
              "startLineNumber": 1,
              "startColumn": 1,
              "endLineNumber": 1,
              "endColumn": 249
            },
            "text": "if there is a instructions directory at  the repository root, is their any hierarchal mechanism to support overriding the instructions or merging them with addition instructions placed at a project root or within a code-workpsace file in a project?",
            "kind": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      "variableData": {
        "variables": [
          {
            "kind": "file",
            "id": "vscode.implicit.viewport",
            "name": "file:ReadMe.md",
            "value": {
              "uri": {
                "$mid": 1,
                "fsPath": "c:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell\\ReadMe.md",
                "_sep": 1,
                "external": "file:///c%3A/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/ReadMe.md",
                "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/ReadMe.md",
                "scheme": "file"
              },
              "range": {
                "startLineNumber": 90,
                "startColumn": 92,
                "endLineNumber": 111,
                "endColumn": 90
              }
            },
            "modelDescription": "User's current visible code"
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": [
        {
          "value": "As of July 2025, **GitHub Copilot’s instruction file mechanism does not support hierarchical merging or overriding** of instructions from multiple `.copilot` directories or from code-workspace files.\n\n### How Copilot Handles Instructions\n\n- **Single Source:** Copilot looks for a `.copilot` directory at the root of the repository. All instructions in this directory apply to the entire repository and all its subfolders/projects.\n- **No Inheritance or Merging:** There is currently **no built-in support** for having additional `.copilot` directories or instruction files in sub-projects or subfolders that would override or merge with the root instructions.\n- **No Workspace File Integration:** Copilot does **not** read or merge instructions from VS Code `.code-workspace` files or from project-specific folders.\n\n### Best Practice\n\n- Place your `.copilot` directory at the repository root.\n- If you need project-specific instructions, include them in the root `.copilot` files and clearly document which instructions apply to which projects (for example, by using headings or sections in your Markdown files).\n\n### Reference\n\n- [GitHub Copilot Workspace Configuration Documentation](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/configuring-copilot/copilot-workspace-configuration)\n\n---\n\n**Summary:**  \nCopilot uses only the root-level `.copilot` directory for instructions. There is no hierarchical override or merge mechanism for project-level or workspace-level instructions at this time.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
      ],
