      "response": [
        {
          "value": "To check if the ProGet service is running on your system, you can use PowerShell to look for the service by name. The ProGet Windows service is typically named **InedoProGet**.\n\nRun this command in PowerShell:\n\n```powershell\nGet-Service -Name InedoProGet\n```\n\nIf the service is running, you will see its status as `Running`.  \nIf it is not running, you will see `Stopped` or an error if the service is not installed.\n\n**Example output:**\n```\nStatus   Name           DisplayName\n------   ----           -----------\nRunning  InedoProGet    ProGet\n```\n\nIf you get an error like `Cannot find any service with service name 'InedoProGet'`, ProGet is not installed or the service name is different.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/",
