    {
      "requestId": "request_2015d875-e3f4-483d-b235-85d2d89a573d",
      "message": {
        "text": "calling Publish-PSResource  results in this excpetion message Repository 'IntPrePSRQAPushFeed': Response status code does not indicate success: 403 (Forbidden).. why?",
        "parts": [
          {
            "range": {
              "start": 0,
              "endExclusive": 166
            },
            "editorRange": {
              "startLineNumber": 1,
              "startColumn": 1,
              "endLineNumber": 1,
              "endColumn": 167
            },
            "text": "calling Publish-PSResource  results in this excpetion message Repository 'IntPrePSRQAPushFeed': Response status code does not indicate success: 403 (Forbidden).. why?",
            "kind": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      "variableData": {
        "variables": [
          {
            "kind": "file",
            "id": "vscode.implicit.selection",
            "name": "file:module.build.ps1",
            "value": {
              "uri": {
                "$mid": 1,
                "fsPath": "c:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell\\module.build.ps1",
                "_sep": 1,
                "external": "file:///c%3A/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/module.build.ps1",
                "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/module.build.ps1",
                "scheme": "file"
              },
              "range": {
                "startLineNumber": 1115,
                "startColumn": 118,
                "endLineNumber": 1115,
                "endColumn": 141,
                "selectionStartLineNumber": 1115,
                "selectionStartColumn": 118,
                "positionLineNumber": 1115,
                "positionColumn": 141
              }
            },
            "modelDescription": "User's active selection"
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": [
        {
          "value": "A `403 (Forbidden)` error from `Publish-PSResource` means **authentication or authorization failed** when trying to publish to the repository `'IntPrePSRQAPushFeed'`. Here are the most common reasons and how to troubleshoot:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **Invalid or Missing API Key**\n- The API key provided via `-ApiKey` is missing, incorrect, expired, or not valid for the target repository.\n- **Check:**  \n  - Is the environment variable for the API key set and correct?  \n    ```powershell\n    [Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable($PSRepositoryFeed.ApiKeyName)\n    ```\n  - Is the key valid for publishing to `'IntPrePSRQAPushFeed'`?\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Insufficient Permissions**\n- The API key or user does not have permission to push packages to the repository.\n- **Check:**  \n  - Does the key/user have \"push\" or \"publish\" rights for this feed?\n  - Are there IP restrictions or other security policies on the server?\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Repository URL or Name Incorrect**\n- The repository name or endpoint is wrong, or does not match what the server expects.\n- **Check:**  \n  - Is `$PSRepositoryFeed.ShortName` and the repository URL correct?\n  - Can you publish manually using the same credentials and URL?\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Repository Configuration**\n- The repository may be read-only, or not configured to accept new packages.\n- **Check:**  \n  - Is the feed enabled for publishing?\n  - Are there any server-side restrictions (e.g., package name, version, or allowed users)?\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Other Causes**\n- Proxy, firewall, or network issues blocking the request.\n- The package already exists and the repository does not allow overwriting.\n\n---\n\n## **How to Troubleshoot**\n\n1. **Verify API Key**\n   - Print the API key (mask sensitive info) and check it matches what the server expects.\n   - Try publishing with the same key using another tool (e.g., `dotnet nuget push` or `nuget.exe push`).\n\n2. **Check Permissions**\n   - Log in to the repository web UI and check the permissions for the API key/user.\n\n3. **Check Repository URL**\n   - Make sure the repository URL and name are correct.\n\n4. **Check Server Logs**\n   - If you control the server, check its logs for more details on the rejection.\n\n5. **Test with a Simple Package**\n   - Try publishing a simple test package to rule out package-specific issues.\n\n---\n\n**Summary:**  \nA `403 Forbidden` means the server rejected your request due to authentication or authorization failure. Double-check your API key, permissions, and repository configuration.\n\nIf you need more help, provide the exact command, the value of `$PSRepositoryFeed`, and how the API key is set.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
      ],
      "responseId": "response_3baa5201-20c8-455c-bd4f-ac61415163c7",
      "result": {
        "timings": {
          "firstProgress": 4052,
          "totalElapsed": 10051
        },
        "metadata": {
          "codeBlocks": [],
          "toolCallRounds": [
            {
              "response": "A `403 (Forbidden)` error from `Publish-PSResource` means **authentication or authorization failed** when trying to publish to the repository `'IntPrePSRQAPushFeed'`. Here are the most common reasons and how to troubleshoot:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **Invalid or Missing API Key**\n- The API key provided via `-ApiKey` is missing, incorrect, expired, or not valid for the target repository.\n- **Check:**  \n  - Is the environment variable for the API key set and correct?  \n    ```powershell\n    [Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable($PSRepositoryFeed.ApiKeyName)\n    ```\n  - Is the key valid for publishing to `'IntPrePSRQAPushFeed'`?\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Insufficient Permissions**\n- The API key or user does not have permission to push packages to the repository.\n- **Check:**  \n  - Does the key/user have \"push\" or \"publish\" rights for this feed?\n  - Are there IP restrictions or other security policies on the server?\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Repository URL or Name Incorrect**\n- The repository name or endpoint is wrong, or does not match what the server expects.\n- **Check:**  \n  - Is `$PSRepositoryFeed.ShortName` and the repository URL correct?\n  - Can you publish manually using the same credentials and URL?\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Repository Configuration**\n- The repository may be read-only, or not configured to accept new packages.\n- **Check:**  \n  - Is the feed enabled for publishing?\n  - Are there any server-side restrictions (e.g., package name, version, or allowed users)?\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Other Causes**\n- Proxy, firewall, or network issues blocking the request.\n- The package already exists and the repository does not allow overwriting.\n\n---\n\n## **How to Troubleshoot**\n\n1. **Verify API Key**\n   - Print the API key (mask sensitive info) and check it matches what the server expects.\n   - Try publishing with the same key using another tool (e.g., `dotnet nuget push` or `nuget.exe push`).\n\n2. **Check Permissions**\n   - Log in to the repository web UI and check the permissions for the API key/user.\n\n3. **Check Repository URL**\n   - Make sure the repository URL and name are correct.\n\n4. **Check Server Logs**\n   - If you control the server, check its logs for more details on the rejection.\n\n5. **Test with a Simple Package**\n   - Try publishing a simple test package to rule out package-specific issues.\n\n---\n\n**Summary:**  \nA `403 Forbidden` means the server rejected your request due to authentication or authorization failure. Double-check your API key, permissions, and repository configuration.\n\nIf you need more help, provide the exact command, the value of `$PSRepositoryFeed`, and how the API key is set.",
              "toolCalls": [],
              "toolInputRetry": 0,
              "id": "8100b1d0-d185-468d-a973-b909c892fe09"
            }
