      },
      "response": [
        {
          "value": "To see the API key for a particular feed in an instance of **Inedo ProGet**, follow these steps:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **Log in to ProGet**\n- Open your ProGet web interface in a browser.\n- Log in with an account that has administrative or appropriate feed management permissions.\n\n### 2. **Navigate to the Feed**\n- Go to **Feeds** in the top menu.\n- Click on the feed you want to view or manage.\n\n### 3. **Check Feed API Keys**\n- In the feed details page, look for a section called **API Keys**, **Connect to Feed**, or **Feed Security**.\n- ProGet does **not** automatically generate a global API key for each feed. Instead, API keys are typically managed per user or per application.\n\n### 4. **User or Application API Keys**\n- Go to **Users & Tasks** > **API Keys** (or **Administration** > **API Keys** in some versions).\n- Here, you can see API keys that have been created, their permissions, and which feeds they apply to.\n- If you need an API key for a specific feed, you may need to **create a new API key** and assign it the appropriate permissions for that feed.\n\n### 5. **Copy or Generate the API Key**\n- If an API key already exists for your user/application and feed, you can view or copy it here.\n- If not, create a new API key, select the feed and permissions, and then copy the generated key.\n\n---\n\n**Note:**  \n- **API keys are sensitive!** Only share them with trusted users or automation.\n- If you do not see the API key section, you may not have sufficient permissions, or your ProGet instance may be using a different authentication method (e.g., Windows Authentication, LDAP, etc.).\n\n---\n\n**Reference:**  \n- [ProGet Documentation: API Keys](https://docs.inedo.com/docs/proget/feeds/api-keys)\n- [ProGet Documentation: Connecting to Feeds](https://docs.inedo.com/docs/proget/feeds/connecting-to-feeds)\n\n---\n\n**Summary:**  \nGo to your feed in ProGet, then to the API Keys section (either in feed settings or under Administration). View, copy, or generate the API key as needed for your feed and user/application.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
      ],
      "responseId": "response_bf8bacab-861b-4b6d-900e-f9bab32de11b",
      "result": {
        "timings": {
          "firstProgress": 4159,
          "totalElapsed": 9106
        },
        "metadata": {
          "codeBlocks": [],
          "toolCallRounds": [
            {
              "response": "To see the API key for a particular feed in an instance of **Inedo ProGet**, follow these steps:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **Log in to ProGet**\n- Open your ProGet web interface in a browser.\n- Log in with an account that has administrative or appropriate feed management permissions.\n\n### 2. **Navigate to the Feed**\n- Go to **Feeds** in the top menu.\n- Click on the feed you want to view or manage.\n\n### 3. **Check Feed API Keys**\n- In the feed details page, look for a section called **API Keys**, **Connect to Feed**, or **Feed Security**.\n- ProGet does **not** automatically generate a global API key for each feed. Instead, API keys are typically managed per user or per application.\n\n### 4. **User or Application API Keys**\n- Go to **Users & Tasks** > **API Keys** (or **Administration** > **API Keys** in some versions).\n- Here, you can see API keys that have been created, their permissions, and which feeds they apply to.\n- If you need an API key for a specific feed, you may need to **create a new API key** and assign it the appropriate permissions for that feed.\n\n### 5. **Copy or Generate the API Key**\n- If an API key already exists for your user/application and feed, you can view or copy it here.\n- If not, create a new API key, select the feed and permissions, and then copy the generated key.\n\n---\n\n**Note:**  \n- **API keys are sensitive!** Only share them with trusted users or automation.\n- If you do not see the API key section, you may not have sufficient permissions, or your ProGet instance may be using a different authentication method (e.g., Windows Authentication, LDAP, etc.).\n\n---\n\n**Reference:**  \n- [ProGet Documentation: API Keys](https://docs.inedo.com/docs/proget/feeds/api-keys)\n- [ProGet Documentation: Connecting to Feeds](https://docs.inedo.com/docs/proget/feeds/connecting-to-feeds)\n\n---\n\n**Summary:**  \nGo to your feed in ProGet, then to the API Keys section (either in feed settings or under Administration). View, copy, or generate the API key as needed for your feed and user/application.",
